Datatype: helps python understand whether the value is a number, text, collection, True/False value etc.
    Python has several buit in datatypes:
1. Integer: used to store whole numbers, without decimal values.
    Example: 10,25,-5,0
    Use: For counting & calculation of whole number

age = 20
print(age)
print(type(age))


2. Float: use to store decimal numbers.
    Example: 10.5,3.14

price: 3.15
print(price)
print(type(price))


3. String: use to store text or a sequence of characters. It is written inside single or double quotes.

name ="Harsh"
print(name)
print(type(name))


4. Boolean: has only two values: True & False

is_student = True
print(is_student)
print(type(is_student))


5. List: use to store multiple values in a single variable. It is ordered & can be changed.
    Example: [80,75]

marks = [1,2,5]
print(marks)
print(type(marks))


6. Tuple: ordered collection of multiple value that can not changed after it is created.
    Example: (10,20,30)

coordinates = (10,20)
print(coordinates)
print(type(coordinates))


7. Set: collection that stores unique values. Duplicate values are automatically removed.
    Example:{10,20,30}

numbers = {10,20,20,30}
print(nummbers)
print(type(numbers))


8. Dictionary: stores data in key value pairs.
   Example:{"name":"Harsh","age":18}

student = {
    "name": "Harsh",
    "age":18
}
print(student)
print(type(student))
